# lintian overrides for the unofficial Qwen Studio deb package (spec §11.3).
#
# Captured against Lintian v2.116.3+deb12u1 running in the debian:12 container
# image (see .github workflows / task B5 report); CI (task C3) runs lintian in
# the same debian:12 image, so this version should stay representative.
#
# Decision rule (spec §11.3): an E: tag may be suppressed here ONLY if it is
# caused by files shipped verbatim from the Electron runtime or the upstream
# Qwen Studio app. Anything about the desktop file, control fields,
# dependencies, maintainer scripts, or file permissions that we control is
# fixed in packaging/electron-builder.base.json instead (see that file, and
# packaging/deb/copyright and scripts/lib/electron-builder-config.ts, for the
# debian-changelog-file-missing-or-wrong-name / no-copyright-file fixes that
# were made there rather than suppressed here; scripts/lib/electron-builder-config.ts's
# stripExecFromSharedLibs() likewise fixes shared-library-is-executable there,
# not here).

# Electron ships its own copies of ffmpeg, EGL/GLES, SwiftShader and Vulkan loaders; they cannot be unbundled.
embedded-library
# Prebuilt Electron binaries and the bun/uv sidecars are not stripped upstream; stripping would break Electron's crash reporting symbols.
unstripped-binary-or-object
# electron-builder installs to /opt/<productName>; this layout is required by the auto-updater and the upstream code.
dir-or-file-in-opt
